    "title": "Word Pattern",
    "workload": "build 8 pattern/subject pairs once (1000 positions each over a 26-letter alphabet, ~4900-char subjects); even pairs are a valid bijection so the full 1000-position loop runs and returns true, odd pairs repeat the FIRST word in the LAST position so they also scan everything before failing -- neither path is an early exit. 2500 punches, sink weights successes by iteration. NOTE: C's letter->word direction is a direct-address array rather than a hash map, and C copies words into a preallocated static buffer where the other four allocate owned strings; both are natural C and both favour it.",
